From de87da6accf064ad3e02f5f0cc4f31abe6b9cd72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:53:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: morph the bottom address bar into the sheet's origin
 pill

In bottom-bar Sheet mode the address bar no longer swaps for a second
pill. One view starts on the location bar's rect and interpolates its
width, height, corner radius, colour and text with the sheet's progress,
riding the sheet's top edge until it parks in the handle row at half.
Drag, open, close and Back all drive the same per-frame update, so it
reverses exactly.

- The travelling pill re-asserts its elevation above the panel and stays
  the root's last child every frame; closing used to drop it to 0, so the
  next open drew it under the actions row and the cards.
- Below half it stays on the root and never trails below the sheet's
  top edge; it parks in the handle row only from half up.
- Opening and closing within the morph range use a standard ease
  (0.4, 0, 0.2, 1) and start on the sheet window's first pre-draw, so
  the slow first frame no longer swallows the morph.

Top-bar mode and the side drawer keep their existing behaviour.
